    "reason": "Hold. ROAS is 4.0 (revenue $4 on $1 spend) and has been flat for all 30 days, so the campaign is efficient and stable. Budget is not the constraint, though: it spends only about $1/day against a $100 cap, so raising the budget would not add spend. The limit is delivery (audience size, bid or cost controls, creative, or placements). To scale, fix those first. Caveats: only about $30 total spend over 30 days is a very small sample, the data stops at 2026-09-30 so Oct 1 is missing, and your breakeven ROAS is unknown."
